Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||06-25-2001||11:26 PM||||Yes there are.<BR>I've heard that the Hypertechs don't do anything but I can tell you the ones ADS makes works.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Don't expect 20 HP though.<BR>Chips can especially wake up an auto. equip'd<BR>car because they hold the gears better.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||venger||06-25-2001||11:31 PM||||Yes there is. I had a chip from the Fiero Store. I didn't see a difference in performance but it should do something. The way to go is the Venom Performance module. It adds up to 25% and you do notice a difference when you floor it. It is listed for a firebird 2.8 MFI. You can check at venomperformance.com<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||06-26-2001||01:39 AM||||Yeah, they're out there.<P>The 2.8L Firebird chip won't work. Don't buy it. That's the 6870 ECM and unless you want to add the mass air flow sensor and swap some wires. Don't.||||reg||1
